speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I wish to table reference No. 174, mover Mr. Diefenbaker:	How
many building or repair contracts have been granted to the Lunam Construction Company, Saskatchewan, since January 1, 1948;
Also reference No. 154, mover Mr. Diefenbaker:	Correspondence between any department of the government and the Lunam Construction Company of Regina, having to do with failure to complete its subcontracts;
Also reference No. 215, mover Mr. Coldwell: Copy of progress reports signed by dominion public works architects, Saskatchewan, in connection with contracts awarded to the Lunam Construction Company of Regina.
This is only a partial report, relating to the Indian hospital at Fort Qu'Appelle. My officials have worked ever since the return was passed in the house to prepare these progress reports, and to have copies photographed and tabled. I had the pleasure of showing the originals to the hon. member for Rosetown-Biggar, and I asked him if he wished to have my officials continue working on these progress reports for all the other contracts, because I do not know if there would be any possibility of tabling them before the end of the session.
